00:11:03,275 --> 00:11:06,206
-Ironically,
that was Bambi's stepmother.

249
00:11:06,241 --> 00:11:07,758
-Honey? Honey?
Where'd you go, honey?

250
00:11:07,793 --> 00:11:09,448
Hun -- honey? Honey?

251
00:11:10,689 --> 00:11:13,931
-[Yawns] I'm just going to
take a little nap.

252
00:11:19,137 --> 00:11:20,758
-Typical deer hunter.

253
00:11:20,793 --> 00:11:22,517
-Yeah, and, meanwhile,
his wife is off watching

254
00:11:22,551 --> 00:11:24,931
the Chippendales
with her girlfriends.

255
00:11:24,965 --> 00:11:31,413
♪♪

256
00:11:31,448 --> 00:11:32,517
-It's okay.

257
00:11:32,551 --> 00:11:36,137
Deer spontaneously
regenerate bodies.

258
00:11:36,172 --> 00:11:38,689
-They're punting
the deer's head!

259
00:11:42,724 --> 00:11:44,034
[Whistle blows]

260
00:11:44,068 --> 00:11:47,551
-They're waving giant tribbles.

261
00:11:47,586 --> 00:11:50,000
-The cheerleaders suggest
that we go!

262
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,137
-I'm going!

263
00:11:54,172 --> 00:11:56,413
The cheerleader's plan
is working!

264
00:11:58,758 --> 00:12:01,517
-Hey, a bearded egg in a tie.

265
00:12:02,758 --> 00:12:04,862
-Black power.

266
00:12:04,896 --> 00:12:06,172
-Go!

267
00:12:06,206 --> 00:12:08,448
Come on!

268
00:12:08,482 --> 00:12:11,655
-Eh, you take it!

269
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:14,413
-Go, go!

270
00:12:14,448 --> 00:12:19,034
-They took our advice
and started winning!

271
00:12:19,068 --> 00:12:23,034
-We have attached our egos
to you!

272
00:12:23,068 --> 00:12:24,586
[Telephone ringing]

273
00:12:24,620 --> 00:12:26,689
-Wow, that antelope
has a lot of degrees.

274
00:12:26,724 --> 00:12:28,310
-Well, Bill, I'd say Arkansas
is in good shape.

275
00:12:28,344 --> 00:12:29,862
-Uh, yeah? Hello?

276
00:12:29,896 --> 00:12:31,517
I mean, Dr. Lockhart's office.

277
00:12:31,551 --> 00:12:33,965
-Yes, I'm skinnier.
-Yep.

278
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,689
-Yes, sir.

279
00:12:35,724 --> 00:12:38,068
-He's at the game, sir.

280
00:12:38,103 --> 00:12:39,413
Get him?

281
00:12:39,448 --> 00:12:42,448
Sir, he's at the stadium
with 75,000 insane hog callers.

282
00:12:42,482 --> 00:12:44,103
-They're calling insane hogs?

283
00:12:44,137 --> 00:12:45,068
-Yes, sir.

284
00:12:45,103 --> 00:12:47,931
All right. Right away, sir.

285
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:54,310
-Your halftime show -- Yo-Yo Ma

286
00:12:54,344 --> 00:12:58,172
and the entire
Bach Cello Suites.

287
00:12:58,206 --> 00:13:01,241
-I'm going to leave in the firstquarter to beat the rush.

288
00:13:05,655 --> 00:13:08,172
-There's a chickpea!

289
00:13:09,206 --> 00:13:12,482
-The stadium is built next to
a giant Braun coffee grinder.

290
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:18,413
-Sir, sir, your fly is open.

291
00:13:18,448 --> 00:13:21,241
I saw it from across the field.

292
00:13:23,482 --> 00:13:25,241
-Well,
just resuscitate the patient.

293
00:13:25,275 --> 00:13:27,551
I'll be there at the half.

294
00:13:28,655 --> 00:13:31,482
-Who was that skinny guy
who just talked to me?

295
00:13:32,689 --> 00:13:34,034
-Go, go, go!

296
00:13:34,068 --> 00:13:37,827
-A Razorback hat lacks the quietdignity of the cheese wedge.

297
00:13:37,862 --> 00:13:40,448
-Mm-hmm.

298
00:13:40,482 --> 00:13:43,068
-We welcome Accountemps
in section four!

299
00:13:43,103 --> 00:13:45,689
-Holding penalty...

300
00:13:45,724 --> 00:13:47,965
[Crowd cheering]

301
00:13:51,206 --> 00:13:54,137
-Get your tongue out of my ear.
What are you...

302
00:13:54,172 --> 00:13:56,862
-I heard that!

303
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,482
-Hmm.

304
00:13:59,517 --> 00:14:04,586
♪♪

305
00:14:06,275 --> 00:14:07,758
-Yes, sir.

306
00:14:07,793 --> 00:14:09,482
-I'm ready for some football.

307
00:14:09,517 --> 00:14:11,896
-Listen,
we appreciate you calling us.

308
00:14:11,931 --> 00:14:14,517
We should be in Texarkana
before dark, yes.

309
00:14:14,551 --> 00:14:15,655
Okay.

310
00:14:15,689 --> 00:14:17,137
Thank you very much. Goodbye.

311
00:14:17,172 --> 00:14:19,034
All right. We got everything --

312
00:14:19,068 --> 00:14:22,827
got the Jeep, camper,
got the computer, mic sensors?

313
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,758
-Everything but the mic sensors.

314
00:14:24,793 --> 00:14:26,620
-Okay.
Where's your friend Leslie?

315
00:14:26,655 --> 00:14:28,310
-She should be here anytime.

316
00:14:28,344 --> 00:14:29,793
-Tim, go ahead
and get the mic sensors.

317
00:14:29,827 --> 00:14:31,931
Put them in.
-Uh, mic's right here!

318
00:14:31,965 --> 00:14:35,103
-Oh, but, uh, all right.

319
00:14:35,137 --> 00:14:37,862
Um...

320
00:14:37,896 --> 00:14:38,931
-Hi!

321
00:14:38,965 --> 00:14:42,655
-It's the keyboardist
from "Fame."

322
00:14:42,689 --> 00:14:44,379
-Anybody tell you
where we're going?

323
00:14:44,413 --> 00:14:45,793
-Yep, Texarkana.

324
00:14:45,827 --> 00:14:48,551
-There's a disco there, right?

325
00:14:48,586 --> 00:14:51,206
-They tell you we're going to bein the woods most of the time?

326
00:14:51,241 --> 00:14:52,689
-Well, she said
we're going down looking for

327
00:14:52,724 --> 00:14:54,034
some kind of wild man.

328
00:14:54,068 --> 00:14:55,068
What?

329
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:56,931
-I am that wild man.

330
00:14:56,965 --> 00:15:00,482
-You just don't look likeyou're dressed for the occasion.

331
00:15:00,517 --> 00:15:01,965
-Well, I brought
my jeans and shorts.

332
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,034
-Uh, will they dress for
the trip?

333
00:15:04,068 --> 00:15:06,275
-I certainly hope so.

334
00:15:06,310 --> 00:15:07,862
Load up and let's go.
-Great.

335
00:15:07,896 --> 00:15:10,931
-Now I'm Bocephus.

336
00:15:10,965 --> 00:15:13,586
-My name is Brian C. Lockhart.

337
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,448
My friends call me Doc,

338
00:15:15,482 --> 00:15:17,103
but I'm a professor of
anthropology at

339
00:15:17,137 --> 00:15:18,413
The University of Arkansas,

340
00:15:18,448 --> 00:15:20,344
located deep
in the Ozark Mountains.

341
00:15:20,379 --> 00:15:21,931
-I'm a dim-witted left.

342
00:15:21,965 --> 00:15:24,241
-With me, one of my freshman
students, Tim Thornton.

343
00:15:24,275 --> 00:15:25,793
-My snap-towel manager.

344
00:15:25,827 --> 00:15:27,482
-Leslie Ann Walker --
All I know about her,

345
00:15:27,517 --> 00:15:30,000
she's a good friend
of Tanya Yazzie,

346
00:15:30,034 --> 00:15:31,206
one of my prized students.

347
00:15:31,241 --> 00:15:32,689
-Prized student in that
she gets C's,

348
00:15:32,724 --> 00:15:35,068
but she's really cute.

349
00:15:35,103 --> 00:15:39,275
♪♪

350
00:15:39,310 --> 00:15:41,448
-We're going camping,
and you're going to watch.

351
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:43,103
-After my call from
the Miller County

352
00:15:43,137 --> 00:15:45,517
Sheriff's Department,
we were soon leaving

353
00:15:45,551 --> 00:15:48,034
the rolling hills
of northern Arkansas behind

354
00:15:48,068 --> 00:15:50,068
and headed for the swamps.

355
00:15:50,103 --> 00:15:52,413
-Hey, the Tomb of the Unknown
Cracker.

356
00:15:56,137 --> 00:15:58,517
-Tim had a bladder the size
of a thimble.

357
00:15:58,551 --> 00:16:03,379
♪♪

358
00:16:03,413 --> 00:16:05,758
-Here's where the legend works
the night shift.

359
00:16:07,793 --> 00:16:10,103
-Even this place
has a great website.

360
00:16:13,655 --> 00:16:15,034
-Can I help y'all?

361
00:16:15,068 --> 00:16:18,103
-Yes, do you sell turquoise
plastic pith helmets?

362
00:16:18,137 --> 00:16:20,068
-Good evening.
-Good evening!

363
00:16:20,103 --> 00:16:22,620
-Do you, uh,
have any ammunition?

364
00:16:22,655 --> 00:16:24,034
-Yes, sir.

365
00:16:24,068 --> 00:16:27,827
-We both forgot our teeth.
-I need a box of .30-30 shells.

366
00:16:27,862 --> 00:16:29,620
-Regular or hollow-point?

367
00:16:29,655 --> 00:16:32,413
-Doesn't matter.

368
00:16:32,448 --> 00:16:34,517
-Want this on
your Klan account?

369
00:16:37,862 --> 00:16:40,517
-Y'all going camping?

370
00:16:40,551 --> 00:16:42,551
-I guess you could say that.

371
00:16:42,586 --> 00:16:45,000
We're looking for
the Boggy Creek Creature.

372
00:16:45,034 --> 00:16:46,551
-I married her!

373
00:16:46,586 --> 00:16:48,034
[Laughs]

374
00:16:48,068 --> 00:16:50,827
[Laughter]

375
00:16:50,862 --> 00:16:53,068
-There ain't no such thing,
you know?

376
00:16:53,103 --> 00:16:55,000
-I know, but we got
this funding.

377
00:16:55,034 --> 00:16:56,379
-I guess that's why we're here.

378
00:16:56,413 --> 00:16:58,689
We're going to try to determine
if there is one or not.

379
00:16:58,724 --> 00:17:00,586
-You can take my word for it.

380
00:17:00,620 --> 00:17:03,482
There ain't no monsters
around here.

381
00:17:03,517 --> 00:17:06,724
-Well, then, do you have any
puffy hats with filthy sayings?

382
00:17:06,758 --> 00:17:09,275
-I believe that's about
all we need.

383
00:17:09,310 --> 00:17:10,551
-Hey, boy, where do you think

384
00:17:10,586 --> 00:17:13,241
you're going to
find that monster?

385
00:17:13,275 --> 00:17:14,724
-Leave me alone, you guys.

386
00:17:14,758 --> 00:17:17,517
-Going to find him in the swamp
if it exists.

387
00:17:17,551 --> 00:17:19,827
-Well, he don't.
-Ooh.

388
00:17:19,862 --> 00:17:23,379
-He's been seen over 100 times
since the early '50s.

389
00:17:23,413 --> 00:17:26,310
-Seen by who,
drunks or city folks like you,

390
00:17:26,344 --> 00:17:28,931
all wanting your names
in the newspaper?

391
00:17:28,965 --> 00:17:30,310
[Laughs]

392
00:17:30,344 --> 00:17:34,758
-Okay, call off your dogs.

393
00:17:34,793 --> 00:17:36,206
-What do I owe you?

394
00:17:36,241 --> 00:17:39,275
-Well, that'll be
$16.59, please.

395
00:17:39,310 --> 00:17:40,793
-You want to contribute
to our fund

396
00:17:40,827 --> 00:17:43,275
for the War Against
Northern Aggression?

397
00:17:46,241 --> 00:17:47,206
-So that's money!

398
00:17:47,241 --> 00:17:49,655
Usually, we get paid
in possum hides.

399
00:17:49,689 --> 00:17:51,793
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

400
00:17:55,310 --> 00:17:57,241
You know something, though?
-I don't like your neck sweat.

401
00:17:57,275 --> 00:18:00,206
-You ought to go down there
to that swamp tonight

402
00:18:00,241 --> 00:18:02,137
with a monkey suit,

403
00:18:02,172 --> 00:18:04,551
and these here folks
would stay tomorrow night

404
00:18:04,586 --> 00:18:06,758
at the motel in the city!

405
00:18:06,793 --> 00:18:08,448
-Well, ain't going
to work now, Earl.

406
00:18:08,482 --> 00:18:10,689
He's standing right there!

407
00:18:10,724 --> 00:18:13,000
[Laughter]

408
00:18:13,034 --> 00:18:15,827
-You know something?

409
00:18:15,862 --> 00:18:17,862
I believe there's
a creature here.

410
00:18:17,896 --> 00:18:20,344
-There it is!
-And being a city fella

411
00:18:20,379 --> 00:18:23,758
like I am,
I'm scared to death of it.

412
00:18:23,793 --> 00:18:26,344
That's why I got a .30-30 rifle
in the back of that Jeep

413
00:18:26,379 --> 00:18:28,172
and I bought
this box of shells.

414
00:18:28,206 --> 00:18:29,724
-Liberal!

415
00:18:29,758 --> 00:18:32,586
-In fact, I'm so afraid of it,

416
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:35,103
I just might shoot a monkey
if it jumped out on me.

417
00:18:35,137 --> 00:18:36,793
-Andy!

418
00:18:36,827 --> 00:18:38,586
-Good day, sir.

419
00:18:38,620 --> 00:18:41,068
-And I will not call again.

420
00:18:41,103 --> 00:18:44,931
♪♪

421
00:18:44,965 --> 00:18:49,620
-♪ On the wings of
a snow-white dove ♪

422
00:18:49,655 --> 00:18:53,344
♪ He sends his pure sweet love

423
00:18:53,379 --> 00:18:55,965
♪ A sign from above

424
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:57,689
-♪ Abo-bove

425
00:18:57,724 --> 00:19:00,620
-It's the Orval Faubus museum.

426
00:19:00,655 --> 00:19:03,241
-I got nipple rub.

427
00:19:03,275 --> 00:19:05,034
-Oh, him.

428
00:19:05,068 --> 00:19:07,241
-That's W.L. Slogan's farm
that we studied about,

429
00:19:07,275 --> 00:19:08,620
right there.
-Dublow?

430
00:19:08,655 --> 00:19:10,310
-You think he'll let us
go look in the barn?

431
00:19:10,344 --> 00:19:12,241
-Yeah, let's go look in it.

432
00:19:12,275 --> 00:19:14,413
-Besides, we might
find something.

433
00:19:14,448 --> 00:19:16,034
-Tim, run up to the farmhouse
and see if they'll let us

434
00:19:16,068 --> 00:19:17,827
go down to the barn
and look around, okay?

435
00:19:17,862 --> 00:19:19,862
-Yeah, threaten them
with your physique.

436
00:19:23,551 --> 00:19:25,862
-Can I borrow a cup of shirt?

437
00:19:28,344 --> 00:19:31,517
-I bet she doesn't want us
around here.

438
00:19:31,551 --> 00:19:34,172
-I don't want you around here.

439
00:19:34,206 --> 00:19:36,517
-Okay. Hey, y'all, come on.

440
00:19:36,551 --> 00:19:38,241
-Come on.

441
00:19:40,379 --> 00:19:43,344
-You guys can use the toilet,
but she says I can't.

442
00:19:45,379 --> 00:19:47,034
-So these three are
all majoring

443
00:19:47,068 --> 00:19:49,137
in Boggy Creek studies?

444
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,482
-And he falls in
and gets eaten by a pig.

445
00:19:56,068 --> 00:20:00,172
-Late in the afternoon,
Slogan came --

446
00:20:00,206 --> 00:20:01,931
that field there,
driving his cows.

447
00:20:01,965 --> 00:20:03,379
-And one of them blew a tire.

448
00:20:03,413 --> 00:20:07,275
-He had to have put them
in that stall right there,

449
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:11,241
but it was in this barn
where he saw the creature.

450
00:20:11,275 --> 00:20:13,379
-Yeah, when you major
in Boggy Creek studies,

451
00:20:13,413 --> 00:20:14,758
you can write your own ticket

452
00:20:14,793 --> 00:20:17,000
on Wall Street
after you graduate, huh?

453
00:20:21,551 --> 00:20:24,448
-Okay, people without shirts,
please put them on,

454
00:20:24,482 --> 00:20:26,931
and people with shirts,
please take them off.

455
00:20:32,655 --> 00:20:35,275
-You know, they said Slogan
was in his late 60s.

456
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:37,482
-God, I said that well.

457
00:20:37,517 --> 00:20:40,862
-I think it was in about
'63 or '64.

458
00:20:40,896 --> 00:20:42,310
-It was '64.

459
00:20:42,344 --> 00:20:45,551
-That's correct.
It was in the fall of the year.

460
00:20:45,586 --> 00:20:46,965
In fact, it was probably about

461
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,137
this time of day,
late afternoon.

462
00:20:49,172 --> 00:20:51,379
-Geez, do a push-up, kid.

463
00:20:51,413 --> 00:20:53,586
-It came in from that field,

464
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:57,896
drove those cows over here
in the stall...

465
00:20:57,931 --> 00:20:59,931
-Turn off the lights and let me
project my thoughts.

466
00:20:59,965 --> 00:21:02,000
-Come on. Get up there.

467
00:21:02,034 --> 00:21:04,379
Get in there.

468
00:21:04,413 --> 00:21:07,413
-You're in so much trouble,
jumping over the moon.

469
00:21:10,931 --> 00:21:13,000
-Have a good time
in there, you two.

470
00:21:16,724 --> 00:21:19,827
-My memory had cheesecloth
over it at this point.

471
00:21:23,655 --> 00:21:24,620
[Rooster crows]

472
00:21:24,655 --> 00:21:25,551
-Sure, crow now.

473
00:21:25,586 --> 00:21:27,206
It's 11:30.

474
00:21:31,103 --> 00:21:33,172
-The cows had a mutilation
they had to go to.

475
00:21:33,206 --> 00:21:35,448
[Door creaks]

476
00:21:35,482 --> 00:21:39,724
♪♪

477
00:21:39,758 --> 00:21:42,275
-If I'm not mistaken,
that's Jed!

478
00:21:42,310 --> 00:21:44,241
-Ah, all right.

479
00:21:44,275 --> 00:21:47,448
-He cuts a dashing figure
in his wife's Panama hat.

480
00:21:47,482 --> 00:21:49,034
-Looks like Tom Wolfe.

481
00:21:49,068 --> 00:21:53,482
♪♪

482
00:21:53,517 --> 00:21:56,689
-Well, no sense closing
the barn door after the cows.

483
00:21:56,724 --> 00:21:58,551
Hey, I invented an aphorism.

484
00:21:58,586 --> 00:22:03,517
♪♪

485
00:22:03,551 --> 00:22:05,137
-Ted Nugent?
-Slash?

486
00:22:05,172 --> 00:22:06,862
-Rob Zombie?

487
00:22:06,896 --> 00:22:08,448
-Cher?
-Yeah, Cher.

488
00:22:08,482 --> 00:22:10,586
[Dog barking in distance]

489
00:22:14,206 --> 00:22:16,724
-Hey, Legend,
how's the continuing going?

490
00:22:21,379 --> 00:22:24,310
-Well, no more corn liquor
on my Total for breakfast.

491
00:22:27,689 --> 00:22:29,000
-Well, I'll be damned.

492
00:22:29,034 --> 00:22:31,068
Farmers do exist.

493
00:22:34,241 --> 00:22:37,034
-I am so much better
than this barn.

494
00:22:40,931 --> 00:22:42,758
♪ Well, we're drivin'
down the road ♪

495
00:22:42,793 --> 00:22:44,172
♪ Looking for a Waffle House

496
00:22:44,206 --> 00:22:46,172
♪ Drinking lots of Wild Turkey,
yeah ♪

497
00:22:46,206 --> 00:22:48,517
-Wee-hoo.

498
00:22:48,551 --> 00:22:50,448
Hoo-hoo.

499
00:22:50,482 --> 00:22:55,724
♪♪

500
00:22:55,758 --> 00:23:00,965
♪♪

501
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:03,275
-Hey, knock it off,
you big lizard.

502
00:23:03,310 --> 00:23:05,103
