for allowing us

1238
00:56:35,827 --> 00:56:38,000
to place
a camera in his helmet.

1239
00:56:40,206 --> 00:56:43,655
-It might get a little cold
before the night is over.

1240
00:56:43,689 --> 00:56:47,586
-We do have a heater
in this thing, don't we?

1241
00:56:47,620 --> 00:56:50,448
-Yep, I believe we do.

1242
00:56:50,482 --> 00:56:51,793
-How much gas we got?

1243
00:56:51,827 --> 00:56:54,206
-We have E gallons.

1244
00:56:56,413 --> 00:56:57,827
-Over half a tank.

1245
00:56:57,862 --> 00:56:58,827
-Good.
-Wait.

1246
00:56:58,862 --> 00:57:01,241
Which half?
-Today is Tuesday.

1247
00:57:01,275 --> 00:57:06,206
They should find us before the
weekend and we run out of gas.

1248
00:57:06,241 --> 00:57:07,758
-You got me into this mess.

1249
00:57:07,793 --> 00:57:10,413
I want to get out,
and I want to go home.

1250
00:57:10,448 --> 00:57:12,172
Alls we've got to do now
is find a tombstone

1251
00:57:12,206 --> 00:57:14,241
to mark the spot
where you buried us.

1252
00:57:14,275 --> 00:57:16,862
-I think the normally
crisp Charles B. Pierce

1253
00:57:16,896 --> 00:57:20,586
writing style
has fallen apart here.

1254
00:57:20,620 --> 00:57:23,724
-Ahh, not looking
for them is great.

1255
00:57:23,758 --> 00:57:25,586
-[Sighs]

1256
00:57:25,620 --> 00:57:28,965
-He's smoking a swizzle stick.

1257
00:57:29,000 --> 00:57:30,241
-It's almost 8:00.

1258
00:57:30,275 --> 00:57:32,068
-Time for "Dharma & Greg."

1259
00:57:32,103 --> 00:57:34,275
-We're going to have
to go find them.

1260
00:57:34,310 --> 00:57:35,517
-How?

1261
00:57:35,551 --> 00:57:37,413
It's 15 miles out
of this bottom.

1262
00:57:37,448 --> 00:57:39,344
-Wow, you could file papers
in that part he has.

1263
00:57:39,379 --> 00:57:43,310
-And remember they have
our only transportation.

1264
00:57:43,344 --> 00:57:46,310
-Where the hell could they be?

1265
00:57:46,344 --> 00:57:49,517
-Leslie probably talked Tanya
into going into town,

1266
00:57:49,551 --> 00:57:52,551
probably looking for something
besides bologna to eat.

1267
00:57:52,586 --> 00:57:54,448
-Tim's humor
falls a little flat.

1268
00:57:54,482 --> 00:57:55,827
-[Chuckles]

1269
00:57:55,862 --> 00:57:57,896
[Wolf howls]

1270
00:57:57,931 --> 00:57:59,172
-Look at that makeup.

1271
00:57:59,206 --> 00:58:01,275
It looks like she's looking out
of a charred log.

1272
00:58:01,310 --> 00:58:04,034
-What was that?
-What was what?

1273
00:58:04,068 --> 00:58:06,655
-That sound we just heard.

1274
00:58:06,689 --> 00:58:08,241
-It sounded like a wolf.

1275
00:58:08,275 --> 00:58:11,137
-A wolf?
-Do you think it will survive?

1276
00:58:11,172 --> 00:58:13,448
-You mean there's wolves
in these woods, too?

1277
00:58:13,482 --> 00:58:16,586
-Also snakes, bobcats,
alligators --

1278
00:58:16,620 --> 00:58:19,517
-That's enough.
Don't tell me anymore.

1279
00:58:19,551 --> 00:58:20,793
-Wolves, where? Where?

1280
00:58:20,827 --> 00:58:22,896
Bobcats, alligators, no, no.

1281
00:58:22,931 --> 00:58:26,034
-God, there's a winch
on the front.

1282
00:58:26,068 --> 00:58:27,137
-What's that?

1283
00:58:27,172 --> 00:58:28,896
-Something that gets you
unstuck with.

1284
00:58:28,931 --> 00:58:32,517
-Well, why in the hell haven't
you mentioned it before now?

1285
00:58:32,551 --> 00:58:33,655
-You didn't ask.

1286
00:58:33,689 --> 00:58:35,379
Besides, I don't know
how to use it.

1287
00:58:35,413 --> 00:58:38,620
-Stupid, we have a manual
right here.

1288
00:58:38,655 --> 00:58:39,862
Hand me the flashlight.

1289
00:58:39,896 --> 00:58:41,724
-Perhaps, they could fashion
their eyeliner

1290
00:58:41,758 --> 00:58:44,482
into a crude spear
for protection.

1291
00:58:44,517 --> 00:58:46,551
-Okay, it says you keep
the motor running.

1292
00:58:46,586 --> 00:58:49,379
You pull --
keep the vehicle in neutral.

1293
00:58:49,413 --> 00:58:51,034
You pull out
on the cable until...

1294
00:58:51,068 --> 00:58:54,172
-And then it just ends.

1295
00:58:54,206 --> 00:58:55,482
-Now I'm lost.

1296
00:58:55,517 --> 00:58:57,137
Where the hell am I?

1297
00:59:04,034 --> 00:59:06,034
-Here we go.

1298
00:59:06,068 --> 00:59:11,482
-I'm going to get that
windshield for you.

1299
00:59:11,517 --> 00:59:13,655
-Apparently Candie's made
a hiking boot.

1300
00:59:13,689 --> 00:59:15,379
-Hmm.

1301
00:59:15,413 --> 00:59:16,862
-Here it is, right here.

1302
00:59:16,896 --> 00:59:19,103
-The ground, right where
it's supposed to be.

1303
00:59:22,413 --> 00:59:26,000
-Hmm, it's a series of symbols
that carry no meaning.

1304
00:59:30,448 --> 00:59:31,931
-See?
There's a cable right there.

1305
00:59:31,965 --> 00:59:33,103
You just pull out on that.

1306
00:59:33,137 --> 00:59:35,655
-Hmm, they're lucky
they get cable out here.

1307
00:59:35,689 --> 00:59:39,068
-I figured I'd be doing
all the work.

1308
00:59:39,103 --> 00:59:41,620
-I'm the Mack Truck bulldog.
Ruff.

1309
00:59:46,241 --> 00:59:48,862
-Two butch-looking women
not in a Subaru?

1310
00:59:48,896 --> 00:59:52,034
Something's wrong here.
-Yeah.

1311
00:59:52,068 --> 00:59:54,137
-Aah!
-Mike, Mike, she's in the mud.

1312
00:59:54,172 --> 00:59:55,758
They have to wrestle.
-No.

1313
00:59:55,793 --> 00:59:57,689
-[Laughing]

1314
00:59:57,724 --> 01:00:00,655
-All her woodland friends
are laughing at her.

1315
01:00:03,689 --> 01:00:06,137
-"McLintock."
-Look, woman.

1316
01:00:06,172 --> 01:00:07,931
If you want to get out of here,
you better get down here

1317
01:00:07,965 --> 01:00:09,413
and help me.

1318
01:00:09,448 --> 01:00:10,965
-Well, I do want
to get out of here.

1319
01:00:11,000 --> 01:00:12,689
-But I enjoy seeing you
in the mud.

1320
01:00:12,724 --> 01:00:16,068
It's a difficult choice.

1321
01:00:16,103 --> 01:00:17,379
-Well, now that
they're in the mud,

1322
01:00:17,413 --> 01:00:19,137
I'm actually feeling
kind of ashamed of myself.

1323
01:00:19,172 --> 01:00:22,068
Is this really what I wanted?

1324
01:00:25,689 --> 01:00:27,137
-That's the brake cable.

1325
01:00:27,172 --> 01:00:29,137
You're pulling it right
out of the car.

1326
01:00:32,655 --> 01:00:35,689
-Ranger Rick goes berserk.

1327
01:00:35,724 --> 01:00:36,862
-They're not shooting day
for night.

1328
01:00:36,896 --> 01:00:39,137
It's more like 4:30 for 5:00.

1329
01:00:43,137 --> 01:00:45,275
-Okay, I'll go talk
to the truck.

1330
01:00:47,724 --> 01:00:52,862
-Now they stumble on the
Rose Law Firm billing records.

1331
01:00:52,896 --> 01:00:55,586
-Well, my boy and I are here
to help you, ladies.

1332
01:01:00,103 --> 01:01:02,310
-They're making
blueberry vermicelli.

1333
01:01:02,344 --> 01:01:04,586
-Mm.

1334
01:01:04,620 --> 01:01:06,655
-You know, I'm at least
as tense as I was during

1335
01:01:06,689 --> 01:01:09,517
"A Very Brady Christmas."
-Hm.

1336
01:01:09,551 --> 01:01:11,241
-Oh, my God, Leslie.

1337
01:01:11,275 --> 01:01:12,448
There he is.

1338
01:01:12,482 --> 01:01:13,517
-He is?
-[Screams]

1339
01:01:13,551 --> 01:01:15,103
-They must have a better camera
than me.

1340
01:01:15,137 --> 01:01:17,172
I can't see a thing.
-Hmm.

1341
01:01:17,206 --> 01:01:18,965
-[Screams]

1342
01:01:19,000 --> 01:01:21,310
-Oh, they must have seen
a swamp mouse.

1343
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:24,551
They should get a swamp chair
and stand on it.

1344
01:01:24,586 --> 01:01:26,965
-[Vocalizing dramatic music]

1345
01:01:27,000 --> 01:01:33,965
♪♪

1346
01:01:34,000 --> 01:01:36,758
-Well, my rowdy friends
never showed up.

1347
01:01:36,793 --> 01:01:40,034
-Doc, what time is it now?

1348
01:01:40,068 --> 01:01:42,310
-Almost 11:00.

1349
01:01:42,344 --> 01:01:44,310
-I feel something's bad wrong.

1350
01:01:44,344 --> 01:01:48,206
-I think I'm feeling better
about us, though.

1351
01:01:48,241 --> 01:01:51,586
-Yeah, so do I.

1352
01:01:51,620 --> 01:01:53,068
I'll tell you what let's do.

1353
01:01:53,103 --> 01:01:54,586
I don't think we can wait
any longer.

1354
01:01:54,620 --> 01:01:56,034
-Oh, yes. Oh -- oh.

1355
01:01:56,068 --> 01:01:57,827
-Take the rifle.

1356
01:01:57,862 --> 01:02:00,655
We're going to the swamp.

1357
01:02:00,689 --> 01:02:02,724
[Monitor beeping]

1358
01:02:02,758 --> 01:02:05,000
-Two ant sections
are attacking.

1359
01:02:07,310 --> 01:02:11,172
-I got a new chest hair today.

1360
01:02:11,206 --> 01:02:15,275
-Software by Roy Bob's Feed
and Software, Texarkana.

1361
01:02:15,310 --> 01:02:17,310
-Is he back?

1362
01:02:17,344 --> 01:02:19,206
-[Chuckles]

1363
01:02:19,241 --> 01:02:21,344
-No, but the girls are.

1364
01:02:21,379 --> 01:02:23,137
-Are you sure?

1365
01:02:23,172 --> 01:02:24,793
-No, but you see how
slow that's moving?

1366
01:02:24,827 --> 01:02:29,310
-Remember, Tanya just had
reconstructive knee surgery.

1367
01:02:29,344 --> 01:02:30,724
-That's him, all right.

1368
01:02:30,758 --> 01:02:33,586
-Get over there.

1369
01:02:33,620 --> 01:02:36,034
Get on the bed.
-Put on something lacy.

1370
01:02:36,068 --> 01:02:39,689
-We're going to play this out.
-And I have to be on the bed?

1371
01:02:39,724 --> 01:02:42,517
Okay.
-It's him, all right.

1372
01:02:42,551 --> 01:02:45,758
Just relax, now.
Let's just watch this a second.

1373
01:02:45,793 --> 01:02:49,241
-I think its rights
is riding piggyback.

1374
01:02:49,275 --> 01:02:53,172
-Playing it out.
-Yeah.

1375
01:02:53,206 --> 01:02:55,517
-Boy, it sure is playing
out, huh?

1376
01:02:55,551 --> 01:02:57,172
-Mm-hmm.
-Yeah.

1377
01:03:00,137 --> 01:03:01,620
-We -- we're --
we're playing it out.

1378
01:03:01,655 --> 01:03:03,862
Don't -- Stay on the bed.

1379
01:03:03,896 --> 01:03:06,379
-Come in, ladies.

1380
01:03:06,413 --> 01:03:08,379
-And so the completely
pointless stretch

1381
01:03:08,413 --> 01:03:11,689
of movie whimpers
out like a small dying rat.

1382
01:03:15,379 --> 01:03:17,379
-Oh, you know,
this is almost too painful,

1383
01:03:17,413 --> 01:03:18,689
this playing it out.
-Mm-hmm.

1384
01:03:18,724 --> 01:03:20,689
-Yeah.

1385
01:03:20,724 --> 01:03:22,310
-You want to tell me about it?

1386
01:03:22,344 --> 01:03:25,068
-I'm going to let her.
-Well, thank you, Tanya.

1387
01:03:25,103 --> 01:03:26,655
Our adventure started
in base camp.

1388
01:03:26,689 --> 01:03:29,482
The rummy Punjabs
were all around us.

1389
01:03:29,517 --> 01:03:31,551
-We stuck the Jeep.

1390
01:03:31,586 --> 01:03:33,275
-Up your, um --
What's that word?

1391
01:03:33,310 --> 01:03:35,896
-That figures.
-That ain't all.

1392
01:03:35,931 --> 01:03:38,689
-Did you wreck it?
-No.

1393
01:03:38,724 --> 01:03:40,344
We saw it.

1394
01:03:40,379 --> 01:03:41,551
-You saw what?

1395
01:03:41,586 --> 01:03:43,758
-I knew they
wouldn't believe us.

1396
01:03:43,793 --> 01:03:46,413
Damn it, Doc, we saw it.

1397
01:03:46,448 --> 01:03:48,137
You and Tim saw it.

1398
01:03:48,172 --> 01:03:51,000
We believed you.
Why can't you believe us?

1399
01:03:51,034 --> 01:03:53,724
-Oh.
-Why can't I believe them?

1400
01:03:53,758 --> 01:03:56,000
Was it my toilet training?

1401
01:03:56,034 --> 01:03:59,620
-Tanya, did you see it?

1402
01:03:59,655 --> 01:04:00,896
-Yeah.

1403
01:04:00,931 --> 01:04:02,137
-She wants me.

1404
01:04:02,172 --> 01:04:03,793
-It wasn't that I didn't
believe them.

1405
01:04:03,827 --> 01:04:05,965
I guess I just wantedto get back at them a little bit

1406
01:04:06,000 --> 01:04:08,827
for what they had put Tim and I
through for the last six hours.

1407
01:04:08,862 --> 01:04:10,551
-[Vocalizing soundtrack music]

1408
01:04:10,586 --> 01:04:13,758
-Hmm?

1409
01:04:13,793 --> 01:04:15,689
-Aw, well you can't surf
in Arkansas.

1410
01:04:15,724 --> 01:04:18,758
Foul.

1411
01:04:18,793 --> 01:04:22,068
-Unfortunately,
he is the lifeguard.

1412
01:04:22,103 --> 01:04:23,275
-I wouldn't drown.

1413
01:04:23,310 --> 01:04:25,379
The rheumatism is acting up.

1414
01:04:25,413 --> 01:04:28,655
-Play in the sand and shut up.
-Howdy.

1415
01:04:28,689 --> 01:04:32,241
-Howdy.
-You going hunting or fishing?

1416
01:04:32,275 --> 01:04:34,862
-Well, we're heading downriver.

1417
01:04:34,896 --> 01:04:36,068
-Well, how are you traveling?

1418
01:04:36,103 --> 01:04:38,448
Are you wading or riding?

1419
01:04:38,482 --> 01:04:40,137
-[Chuckles]
Hopefully, be riding.

1420
01:04:40,172 --> 01:04:42,034
Do you rent any boats?

1421
01:04:42,068 --> 01:04:45,000
-I got one I can rent you
$5 an hour,

1422
01:04:45,034 --> 01:04:47,413
and I've got a larger boat
I can rent you for $25 a day.

1423
01:04:47,448 --> 01:04:49,344
Everything furnished.

1424
01:04:49,379 --> 01:04:51,103
-We'll take the one
for all day.

1425
01:04:51,137 --> 01:04:52,862
-Good.
-Big spend.

1426
01:04:52,896 --> 01:04:53,931
-You all go right down there
and wait,

1427
01:04:53,965 --> 01:04:55,379
and I'll go bring it around.

1428
01:04:55,413 --> 01:04:57,379
-I just got
to build it first.

1429
01:04:57,413 --> 01:05:03,482
♪♪

1430
01:05:03,517 --> 01:05:09,517
♪♪

1431
01:05:09,551 --> 01:05:11,586
-Okay, let's move them out.

1432
01:05:14,103 --> 01:05:15,241
-Servo, what are you doing?

1433
01:05:15,275 --> 01:05:17,172
-Oh, I've taken up
whittling, Mike.

1434
01:05:17,206 --> 01:05:19,448
-Oh, uh, whittling,
like the guy in the movie?

1435
01:05:19,482 --> 01:05:20,724
-Well, not exactly, no.

1436
01:05:20,758 --> 01:05:22,827
-You see, whittling technology
has been stagnant,

1437
01:05:22,862 --> 01:05:24,413
so we saw an opportunity.

1438
01:05:24,448 --> 01:05:27,034
-We moved in, bought a
little outfit in Kentucky --

1439
01:05:27,068 --> 01:05:28,413
Hey, why is that line stopped?!

1440
01:05:28,448 --> 01:05:29,551
-Somebody got their hair
caught on the line.

1441
01:05:29,586 --> 01:05:31,724
-I don't care. Get it going!
-Okay.

1442
01:05:31,758 --> 01:05:34,689
-Well, now we've got
14,000 employees and 23 plants,

1443
01:05:34,724 --> 01:05:35,965
mostly overseas,

1444
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:37,655
but I still got
the one in the States.

1445
01:05:37,689 --> 01:05:39,241
You know?
-Yeah.

1446
01:05:39,275 --> 01:05:41,034
Wow, you know,
all this machinery,

1447
01:05:41,068 --> 01:05:43,103
all these people,
and what do you make?

1448
01:05:43,137 --> 01:05:45,310
-Well, listen, the product
has always been good.

1449
01:05:45,344 --> 01:05:47,137
We have not altered
the product at all.

1450
01:05:47,172 --> 01:05:49,827
We provide the same stick that'sa little narrower at one end.

1451
01:05:49,862 --> 01:05:50,689
Go ahead.

1452
01:05:50,724 --> 01:05:51,931
Keep that one.
-Thanks.

1453
01:05:51,965 --> 01:05:53,068
-Oh, that's Brazilian mahogany,
by the way.

1454
01:05:53,103 --> 01:05:54,206
It whittles fairly well.

1455
01:05:54,241 --> 01:05:55,793
-Mm, Brazilian mahogany.

1456
01:05:55,827 --> 01:05:58,310
Servo, you're decimating
the rainforest to make these?

1457
01:05:58,344 --> 01:06:00,275
-Oh, listen, Sting,

1458
01:06:00,310 --> 01:06:02,379
you want to see
the cost figures?

1459
01:06:02,413 --> 01:06:03,724
-Uh, you know, I guess
you got to say, it's, uh --

1460
01:06:03,758 --> 01:06:04,931
-Union!

1461
01:06:04,965 --> 01:06:06,034
...it's sort of lost
some of the charm,

1462
01:06:06,068 --> 01:06:07,206
some of the folksiness
that I was --

1463
01:06:07,241 --> 01:06:08,931
-Yeah, hold on.
Hey, get back to work!

1464
01:06:08,965 --> 01:06:10,310
[Workers chanting "Union"]

1465
01:06:10,344 --> 01:06:12,448
-Oh, yeah, sure, like
that's going to happen.

1466
01:06:12,482 --> 01:06:13,931
Call the Pinkertons for me,
will you, Mike?

1467
01:06:13,965 --> 01:06:15,448
I got to go get the hose.

1468
01:06:15,482 --> 01:06:16,448
-Uh, we'll be right back.

1469
01:06:16,482 --> 01:06:17,655
-Unio-- Ow!
-Yeah, union.

1470
01:06:17,689 --> 01:06:20,275
Take a swim, you mutts.

1471
01:06:20,310 --> 01:06:24,034
[Laughing maniacally]

1472
01:06:24,068 --> 01:06:29,137
♪♪

1473
01:06:30,655 --> 01:06:32,827
-Hey, look at that,
a whole beach

1474
01:06:32,862 --> 01:06:34,448
full of research assistants.

1475
01:06:34,482 --> 01:06:35,620
[Chuckles]

1476
01:06:35,655 --> 01:06:40,896
♪♪

1477
01:06:40,931 --> 01:06:43,413
-Ten-hut!

1478
01:06:43,448 --> 01:06:46,000
-How far is it down
to Crenshaw?

1479
01:06:46,034 --> 01:06:47,586
-Well, according
to Deputy Williams,

1480
01:06:47,620 --> 01:06:49,758
it's about 2 miles downriver.

1481
01:06:49,793 --> 01:06:51,275
-Tanya, we should've brought
our swimsuits

1482
01:06:51,310 --> 01:06:53,206
